        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Finiteness and order of the cokernel of a square integer matrix",
        "deps": [],
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "justified_by": [],
        "statement": "For a finite square integer matrix A, coker(A) = Z^n/AZ^n is finite if and only if det(A) is nonzero, and then its order is |det(A)|. For the empty 0 by 0 matrix, the determinant is 1 and the cokernel is the trivial group.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-generated"
        },
        "strategy": "Reduce by unimodular integer row and column operations to a diagonal matrix and compute its cokernel."
