        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let K be a smooth oriented knot in S^3 with chosen compact exterior E_K and positive meridian mu, and let q be an integer at least 2. The homomorphism pi_1(E_K) -> H_1(E_K; Z) -> Z/q sends mu to 1. Let E_q -> E_K be the connected q-sheeted cover classified by its kernel. Attach a solid torus to the torus boundary of E_q so that the meridian disk boundary is the closed lift of mu^q; the resulting oriented closed 3-manifold is the q-fold cyclic branched cover Sigma_q(K). Its deck transformation extends over the filling, and its quotient map to S^3 is branched along K with local model (z,w) -> (z,w^q).",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
