        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let K bound a connected compact oriented Seifert surface F of genus g, choose a disk-band decomposition of F with one 0-handle and 2g bands, and use its band-core basis a_1,...,a_{2g} to form the positive-push Seifert matrix V. For q at least 2, define M_q(V) to have 2g by 2g diagonal blocks V+V^T, upper adjacent blocks -V^T, lower adjacent blocks -V, and all other blocks zero. Push the interior of F into B^4 while keeping K on S^3, cut B^4 along a thickened copy of F, take q copies, and glue the positive face of copy i to the negative face of copy i+1 by reflection of the normal coordinate for i=1,...,q-1, with no last-to-first gluing. Call the resulting q-fold cyclic branched cover W_q(F). Then W_q(F) has one 0-handle and 2g(q-1) 2-handles whose framed attaching link has linking matrix M_q(V), and its boundary branch cover is Sigma_q(K).",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-generated"
